1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,766
On the morning of day three, my water bottle was empty.

2
00:00:04,316 --> 00:00:06,155
I'd finished it during the night.

3
00:00:06,705 --> 00:00:09,131
My mouth was dry, and I had a headache.

4
00:00:09,481 --> 00:00:13,004
When I stood up, I felt dizzy and held the wall until it passed.

5
00:00:13,554 --> 00:00:15,393
My ankle was still swollen.

6
00:00:15,743 --> 00:00:17,544
My hand hurt when I closed it.

7
00:00:18,094 --> 00:00:21,706
Yesterday, I'd walked to the evacuation point and back for nothing.

8
00:00:22,056 --> 00:00:24,928
Today, I needed to find water close to the room.

9
00:00:25,478 --> 00:00:27,623
I couldn't manage another long trip.

10
00:00:28,173 --> 00:00:31,211
I put the empty bottle in my bag and went outside.

11
00:00:31,761 --> 00:00:34,034
There was a small sink behind the shops.

12
00:00:34,584 --> 00:00:35,913
I turned the tap.

13
00:00:36,463 --> 00:00:39,552
A little air came out, followed by a few brown drops.

14
00:00:39,902 --> 00:00:40,989
Then nothing.

15
00:00:41,539 --> 00:00:43,850
I tried another tap on a nearby house.

16
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,848
That one was dry too.

17
00:00:46,398 --> 00:00:50,252
I didn't know whether the water had been shut off or something had stopped working.

18
00:00:50,802 --> 00:00:53,700
Either way, I wasn't getting any from those taps.

19
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:56,918
There was water in the gutter, but it was dirty.

20
00:00:57,268 --> 00:00:58,559
I left it alone.

21
00:00:59,109 --> 00:01:01,828
I needed somewhere water might still be stored.

22
00:01:02,378 --> 00:01:05,671
A small restaurant behind the shops had its back door open.

23
00:01:06,221 --> 00:01:08,992
I listened outside, then stepped into the kitchen.

24
00:01:09,542 --> 00:01:12,529
There were pans on the stove and plates beside the sink.

25
00:01:13,079 --> 00:01:14,420
I tried the stove.

26
00:01:14,770 --> 00:01:17,260
The knob clicked, but no gas came out.

27
00:01:17,810 --> 00:01:19,101
I checked the tap.

28
00:01:19,451 --> 00:01:20,257
Nothing.

29
00:01:20,807 --> 00:01:24,457
The cupboards held cleaning products and a few empty food containers.

30
00:01:24,807 --> 00:01:26,684
I found no bottled drinks.

31
00:01:27,234 --> 00:01:29,864
At the end of a short corridor was a toilet.

32
00:01:30,414 --> 00:01:34,345
I remembered that the tank behind it held water separately from the bowl.

33
00:01:34,695 --> 00:01:35,922
I went to check.

34
00:01:36,472 --> 00:01:39,791
As I lifted the lid, the ceramic scraped against the edge.

35
00:01:40,341 --> 00:01:41,313
I stopped.

36
00:01:41,863 --> 00:01:46,304
After listening for a while, I wrapped some cloth around the lid and lifted it carefully.

37
00:01:46,854 --> 00:01:48,936
The water inside was bright blue.

38
00:01:49,486 --> 00:01:51,720
There was a cleaning tablet at the bottom.

39
00:01:52,270 --> 00:01:53,663
I put the lid back.

40
00:01:54,213 --> 00:01:55,822
I wasn't drinking that.

41
00:01:56,372 --> 00:01:58,926
I checked the remaining cupboard on my way out.

42
00:01:59,276 --> 00:02:00,770
Still nothing useful.

43
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:04,397
I'd spent time searching and had no water to show for it.

44
00:02:04,947 --> 00:02:07,092
Across the lane was a small clinic.

45
00:02:07,642 --> 00:02:09,188
I'd passed it before.

46
00:02:09,538 --> 00:02:13,813
A clinic would have a staff room and bathrooms, and it was small enough to check quickly.

47
00:02:14,163 --> 00:02:16,398
This time, I walked around the outside.

48
00:02:16,948 --> 00:02:18,762
The front entrance was glass.

49
00:02:19,112 --> 00:02:21,652
A metal side door opened onto the lane.

50
00:02:22,202 --> 00:02:25,547
At the back, three infected stood between parked cars.

51
00:02:26,097 --> 00:02:28,344
I stayed behind a dumpster and watched.

52
00:02:28,894 --> 00:02:30,503
They weren't coming toward me.

53
00:02:30,853 --> 00:02:33,955
The corner of the building blocked their view of the side door.

54
00:02:34,505 --> 00:02:36,880
I could leave them alone if I stayed quiet.

55
00:02:37,430 --> 00:02:39,231
I tried the side-door handle.

56
00:02:39,781 --> 00:02:40,753
Unlocked.

57
00:02:41,303 --> 00:02:44,456
Inside was a short corridor leading toward reception.

58
00:02:45,006 --> 00:02:48,197
Before searching, I went to the front entrance and checked it.

59
00:02:48,547 --> 00:02:50,055
That door opened too.

60
00:02:50,605 --> 00:02:55,403
I closed it again and locked it from the inside, so nothing could push it open from the street.

61
00:02:55,953 --> 00:02:57,932
Now I knew both exits worked.

62
00:02:58,482 --> 00:03:02,337
I returned to the side door and wedged it open with folded cardboard.

63
00:03:02,687 --> 00:03:05,023
Then I started checking the rooms nearby.

64
00:03:05,573 --> 00:03:08,280
There was enough daylight to see without the flashlight.

65
00:03:08,830 --> 00:03:11,167
The first room held cleaning supplies.

66
00:03:11,517 --> 00:03:14,504
The next was a staff room with an empty water cooler.

67
00:03:15,054 --> 00:03:18,245
Beside it were three empty plastic bottles with their caps.

68
00:03:18,795 --> 00:03:19,843
I took them.

69
00:03:20,393 --> 00:03:23,342
In a drawer, I found a box of sugar sachets.

70
00:03:23,692 --> 00:03:25,531
I put those in my bag too.

71
00:03:26,081 --> 00:03:27,755
There was no proper food.

72
00:03:28,305 --> 00:03:31,368
Farther along the corridor, I found a utility room.

73
00:03:31,918 --> 00:03:34,344
Inside stood a large hot-water tank.

74
00:03:34,894 --> 00:03:38,022
I'd seen a similar one drained in a place I used to rent.

75
00:03:38,372 --> 00:03:43,017
I hadn't done the job myself, but I remembered there had been a lot of water inside.

76
00:03:43,567 --> 00:03:45,368
This one might still hold some.

77
00:03:45,918 --> 00:03:49,466
I found the drain near the bottom and positioned my bottle beneath it.

78
00:03:49,816 --> 00:03:51,630
I turned the valve by hand.

79
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:55,052
When I tried it, the pipe gave several loud knocks.

80
00:03:55,602 --> 00:03:57,148
I stopped immediately.

81
00:03:57,698 --> 00:04:00,863
I could still picture the three infected behind the building.

82
00:04:01,413 --> 00:04:02,730
I stood listening.

83
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:05,336
No footsteps in the corridor.

84
00:04:05,686 --> 00:04:07,589
No noise from either entrance.

85
00:04:08,139 --> 00:04:11,521
After a while, I tried again, opening it only slightly.

86
00:04:12,071 --> 00:04:15,543
This time, water trickled into the bottle without more knocking.

87
00:04:16,093 --> 00:04:17,983
The first water looked cloudy.

88
00:04:18,333 --> 00:04:21,269
I let that run into a bucket already on the floor.

89
00:04:21,819 --> 00:04:23,875
The water after it looked clearer.

90
00:04:24,425 --> 00:04:27,093
That didn't tell me whether it was safe to drink.

91
00:04:27,643 --> 00:04:29,304
I had no way to check it.

92
00:04:29,654 --> 00:04:35,358
I had a lighter, but the restaurant stove didn't work, and a fire would mean smoke and light I didn't want to risk.

93
00:04:35,908 --> 00:04:37,989
I thought about looking somewhere else.

94
00:04:38,539 --> 00:04:43,210
But I'd found nothing at the shops or the restaurant, and my ankle was already hurting more.

95
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:44,872
I drank some.

96
00:04:45,422 --> 00:04:48,486
Then I filled my bottle and the three I'd found in the staff room.

97
00:04:49,036 --> 00:04:50,709
I kept stopping to listen.

98
00:04:51,259 --> 00:04:52,805
The water ran slowly.

99
00:04:53,155 --> 00:04:56,639
By the time I finished, I'd been inside much longer than planned.

100
00:04:57,189 --> 00:04:59,016
I had four full bottles.

101
00:04:59,566 --> 00:05:01,354
I should have packed them and left.

102
00:05:01,904 --> 00:05:03,488
Instead, I stayed.

103
00:05:04,038 --> 00:05:08,619
I was tired, and I didn't want to leave water behind when I might struggle to find more.

104
00:05:09,169 --> 00:05:11,532
I sat beside the tank and drank again.

105
00:05:12,082 --> 00:05:13,717
Then I rested my ankle.

106
00:05:14,267 --> 00:05:16,450
I told myself I'd leave in a minute.

107
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,413
Nothing had happened since the pipes knocked.

108
00:05:19,763 --> 00:05:21,909
That made it easier to keep waiting.

109
00:05:22,459 --> 00:05:24,068
My bag was still open.

110
00:05:24,418 --> 00:05:26,245
The bottles were on the floor.

111
00:05:26,795 --> 00:05:30,203
When I finally started packing, I heard a thump from reception.

112
00:05:30,753 --> 00:05:31,826
Then another.

113
00:05:32,376 --> 00:05:34,445
Something was hitting the front door.

114
00:05:34,995 --> 00:05:36,745
I looked down the corridor.

115
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:40,576
Through reception, I could see figures against the glass.

116
00:05:41,126 --> 00:05:44,100
I couldn't tell whether they were the ones from the car park.

117
00:05:44,650 --> 00:05:46,196
I didn't wait to count.

118
00:05:46,746 --> 00:05:48,712
I put three bottles in my bag.

119
00:05:49,062 --> 00:05:51,616
That was all I could carry without slowing down.

120
00:05:51,966 --> 00:05:54,149
The fourth was still beside the tank.

121
00:05:54,699 --> 00:05:56,985
Another impact shook the front door.

122
00:05:57,535 --> 00:06:02,027
I left the bottle, pulled the bag onto my shoulder, and headed for the side exit.

123
00:06:02,577 --> 00:06:04,914
The cardboard was still holding it open.

124
00:06:05,464 --> 00:06:08,387
As I reached the door, I heard glass break behind me.

125
00:06:08,937 --> 00:06:12,536
I stepped outside, pulled out the cardboard, and closed the door.

126
00:06:13,086 --> 00:06:15,244
Then I moved away from the car park.

127
00:06:15,794 --> 00:06:18,080
The bottles knocked together in my bag.

128
00:06:18,630 --> 00:06:22,115
I stopped behind a parked van and pushed my spare shirt between them.

129
00:06:22,665 --> 00:06:23,611
I listened.

130
00:06:24,161 --> 00:06:28,015
There were noises from the clinic, but no footsteps coming along the lane.

131
00:06:28,565 --> 00:06:29,741
I kept moving.

132
00:06:30,291 --> 00:06:33,087
At the next corner, I stopped behind a wall.

133
00:06:33,637 --> 00:06:36,267
I'd got out through the second exit I'd checked.

134
00:06:36,817 --> 00:06:38,248
That part had worked.

135
00:06:38,798 --> 00:06:42,627
But I'd wasted time sitting beside the water when I could already have left.

136
00:06:43,177 --> 00:06:44,633
I opened my notes.

137
00:06:45,183 --> 00:06:47,966
Rule three: Once you have what you need, leave.

138
00:06:48,516 --> 00:06:50,687
I hadn't needed to empty the tank.

139
00:06:51,237 --> 00:06:53,765
I hadn't needed to rest inside that building.

140
00:06:54,315 --> 00:06:57,289
I'd needed water, and I'd had it packed within reach.

141
00:06:57,839 --> 00:07:01,043
Staying longer had cost me a bottle and nearly trapped me.

142
00:07:01,593 --> 00:07:05,320
From behind a van on the route home, I could see the clinic entrance.

143
00:07:05,870 --> 00:07:07,595
The front glass was broken.

144
00:07:08,145 --> 00:07:12,127
Several infected were inside reception, with more standing outside.

145
00:07:12,677 --> 00:07:16,633
I didn't know whether the pipes had attracted them or they'd simply wandered over.

146
00:07:17,183 --> 00:07:19,009
I wasn't going back to check.

147
00:07:19,559 --> 00:07:24,473
There was still water in the tank, but reaching it now meant entering a building occupied by them.

148
00:07:25,023 --> 00:07:28,188
I'd have to find another source before these bottles ran out.

149
00:07:28,738 --> 00:07:31,228
I took the quieter streets back to the room.

150
00:07:31,778 --> 00:07:35,658
My ankle hurt, so I walked slowly and kept the bag close to my back.

151
00:07:36,208 --> 00:07:39,845
I checked outside the room, went in, and slid the bolt across.

152
00:07:40,395 --> 00:07:42,515
Then I set the bottles on the floor.

153
00:07:43,065 --> 00:07:45,606
Three bottles, about half a liter each.

154
00:07:46,156 --> 00:07:48,301
I'd also had a drink at the clinic.

155
00:07:48,851 --> 00:07:53,764
It was the first time that morning I could sit down without immediately thinking about getting water.

156
00:07:54,314 --> 00:07:57,352
I still didn't know whether drinking it would make me sick.

157
00:07:57,902 --> 00:08:00,252
There was nothing I could do about that now.

158
00:08:00,802 --> 00:08:02,832
I counted the sugar sachets.

159
00:08:03,182 --> 00:08:04,371
Around thirty.

160
00:08:04,921 --> 00:08:07,270
I ate one, then put the rest away.

161
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,315
I still needed food.

162
00:08:09,665 --> 00:08:11,963
Sugar wasn't going to replace meals.

163
00:08:12,513 --> 00:08:14,990
My ankle was more swollen after the walk.

164
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:17,677
I took off my shoe and rested my foot.

165
00:08:18,227 --> 00:08:20,857
Tomorrow, I would have to keep any trip short.

166
00:08:21,407 --> 00:08:25,083
Before lying down, I packed the bottles so they couldn't knock together.

167
00:08:25,433 --> 00:08:28,152
I put the lighter and flashlight where I could reach them.

168
00:08:28,702 --> 00:08:30,732
Today hadn't fixed everything.

169
00:08:31,282 --> 00:08:35,851
But I'd brought water back, and I'd used the second exit instead of getting stuck inside.

170
00:08:36,401 --> 00:08:38,916
For now, that was enough to let me rest.

171
00:08:39,466 --> 00:08:42,338
That night, footsteps passed outside the door.

172
00:08:42,888 --> 00:08:44,332
They stopped for a while.

173
00:08:44,882 --> 00:08:46,173
I stayed quiet.

174
00:08:46,723 --> 00:08:48,970
After a few moments, they moved on.

175
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:51,410
Later, my stomach cramped.

176
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:53,621
It could have been the water.

177
00:08:53,971 --> 00:08:56,384
It could just as easily have been hunger.

178
00:08:56,734 --> 00:08:58,165
I couldn't tell which.

179
00:08:58,715 --> 00:09:01,944
I lay still on the cardboard, listening to the door.

180
00:09:02,494 --> 00:09:05,099
If it was the water, I would know by morning.

181
00:09:05,449 --> 00:09:08,678
And if I was sick, I wouldn't be going anywhere tomorrow.
